# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# The working clone is on Windows; without this, every text file in a fresh
# checkout shows as modified (CRLF in the worktree vs LF in the index) and any
# `git add -A` sweeps 60+ unrelated files into the commit. Part 2 commits need
# to be readable diffs, so this is set before Layer 2 begins.
#
# After adding this file, run once (see docs/DEVLOG.md):
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git status          # expect: nothing to commit, working tree clean
* text=auto

# Explicit for the file types in this repo.
*.py    text diff=python
*.md    text
*.json  text
*.toml  text
*.patch text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
